  "title": "End of the Ottoman Empire and founding of the Turkish Republic",
  "summary": "After the Turkish War of National Independence, the sultanate was abolished by a vote of the Grand National Assembly in November 1922, ending Ottoman imperial rule. The Republic of Turkey was officially declared on 29 October 1923, with Ankara as its capital and Mustafa Kemal Atatürk as its first president. His regime rested on principles that included nationalism, republicanism and secularism.",
